# {{PROJECT_NAME}}

A production-shaped Drogular PWA starter generated with Drogular {{DROGULAR_VERSION}}.

It already includes:

- a web app manifest;
- a root-scoped service worker;
- offline navigation fallback;
- installable app metadata and icons;
- a responsive starter UI built with a reusable Component.

## Build

```bash
cmake -S . -B build
cmake --build build
```

## Run

```bash
./build/{{PROJECT_NAME}}
```

Open http://localhost:8080/.

For PWA installation and service workers, use a browser context that allows them (localhost is suitable for development).

## Project Structure

- `src/main.cpp` — application setup and PWA registration.
- `src/home_page.hpp` — the home route and PWA page metadata.
- `src/offline_page.hpp` — dynamic offline fallback page.
- `src/components/` — reusable UI components.
- `templates/` — layouts, pages, and component templates.
- `public/manifest.webmanifest` — installable app metadata.
- `public/service-worker.js` — app-shell cache and offline navigation fallback.
- `public/*.svg` — starter app icons.

## Next Steps

- Replace the starter content in `templates/components/app_shell.html`.
- Update the app name, colors, and icon artwork in `public/` before publishing.
- Add pages and reusable Components as the application grows.
- Bump `CACHE_NAME` in `public/service-worker.js` when changing cached app-shell assets.

Tip: keep the service worker small and explicit; cache only assets your application really needs offline.
